  "title": "Wall-Sun-Sun primes and Fibonacci divisibility",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture For any prime $p$, there exists a Fibonacci number divisible by $p$ exactly once.\n\nEquivalently:\n\nConjecture For any prime $p>5$, $p^2$ does not divide $F_{p-\\left(\\frac p5\\right)}$ where $\\left(\\frac mn\\right)$ is the Legendre symbol.",
